(7658322, 1247437, 86447, '<td valign="top">Way to go, Irene!!<br/> <br/>I love this.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your BLUE, friend!<br/></td>', 'Way to go, Irene!! I love this. Congratulations on your BLUE, friend!', '2020-04-13 11:27:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(7658324, 1247437, 103142, '<td valign="top">Doesn''t surprise me in the slightest that this was yours. I do love your lighting!! You should hold a masterclass video on your techniques for all of us who are stranded at home. :)<br/> <br/>Huge congrats on the blue!</td>', 'Doesn''t surprise me in the slightest that this was yours. I do love your lighting!! You should hold a masterclass video on your techniques for all of us who are stranded at home. :) Huge congrats on the blue!', '2020-04-13 11:33:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(7658326, 1247452, 103142, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roz:</b></div><hr/><i> you and Irene got my highest scores .. two of my favourites in the challenge . there were a couple of others i really really liked that didnt do so well tho .. <br/>anyway .. many congratulations on such a brilliant image .. <br/>its truly a magic shot .. will be looking forward to finding out how you did this . <br/>are you a cat whisperer by any chance .. <br/>and is cat whispering something you can learn .. and can it be converted to dog whispering .. xx </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hehe -- no secret -- It is a very large crock. <br/> <br/>The difficult part was that Mo didn''t want to go in the crock. Jeff finally picked him up and put him in it. Once he realized that there was some canned chicken in the bottom, he didn''t mind as much. However, then he would completely disappear. When he was tired of the chicken, he would look out and get out right away. I think I only had 2-3 usable shots from about 25 minutes of shooting!</td>', 'Originally posted by roz: you and Irene got my highest scores .. two of my favourites in the challenge . there were a couple of others i really really liked that didnt do so well tho .. anyway .. many congratulations on such a brilliant image .. its truly a magic shot .. will be looking forward to finding out how you did this . are you a cat whisperer by any chance .. and is cat whispering something you can learn .. and can it be converted to dog whispering .. xx   Hehe -- no secret -- It is a very large crock.  The difficult part was that Mo didn''t want to go in the crock. Jeff finally picked him up and put him in it. Once he realized that there was some canned chicken in the bottom, he didn''t mind as much. However, then he would completely disappear. When he was tired of the chicken, he would look out and get out right away. I think I only had 2-3 usable shots from about 25 minutes of shooting!', '2020-04-13 11:39:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(7658327, 1246983, 103142, '<td valign="top">It was an 8 from me. Beautifully done with a difficult technique. (white on white without reflections!)</td>', 'It was an 8 from me. Beautifully done with a difficult technique. (white on white without reflections!)', '2020-04-13 11:40:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(7658331, 1247454, 103142, '<td valign="top">I really loved this, but I wasn''t sure about the arms disappearing into the background. I wish there was a hint of the figure or that it was cropped in or something. But the rest of it was lovely and even a bit haunting.</td>', 'I really loved this, but I wasn''t sure about the arms disappearing into the background. I wish there was a hint of the figure or that it was cropped in or something. But the rest of it was lovely and even a bit haunting.', '2020-04-13 11:42:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7658332, 1247463, 103142, '<td valign="top">Hmmm -- that shows a different of opinions on what fits the challenge. I''d say this is much more crockery than the white plates that took third. (I voted on the third place like it did fit the definition, even though in mind mind crockery is more earthenware.)<br/> <br/>I''m glad when people make comments like these. It reinforces that everyone has different opinions. :)<br/> <br/>Anyway, I love your lighting and setup on this! Simple but very effective.</td>', 'Hmmm -- that shows a different of opinions on what fits the challenge. I''d say this is much more crockery than the white plates that took third. (I voted on the third place like it did fit the definition, even though in mind mind crockery is more earthenware.) I''m glad when people make comments like these. It reinforces that everyone has different opinions. :) Anyway, I love your lighting and setup on this! Simple but very effective.', '2020-04-13 11:45:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7658333, 1247446, 103142, '<td valign="top">Lovely! I enjoy the brown tones carried throughout. Congrats on the top ten!</td>', 'Lovely! I enjoy the brown tones carried throughout. Congrats on the top ten!', '2020-04-13 11:45:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7658336, 1247015, 103142, '<td valign="top">I like everything except the spoon. With placing the egg that far out to the right, it seems to interrupt the flow of how you look through the photo. If it had been turned about 150 degrees and had the egg coming out towards the left, I think it would have felt more balanced.<br/> <br/>That being said, the rest is quite lovely!!</td>', 'I like everything except the spoon. With placing the egg that far out to the right, it seems to interrupt the flow of how you look through the photo. If it had been turned about 150 degrees and had the egg coming out towards the left, I think it would have felt more balanced. That being said, the rest is quite lovely!!', '2020-04-13 11:47:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(7658355, 1247437, 24454, '<td valign="top">Of COURSE this won.. and of COURSE its yours.  Irene, what a gift to be able to make the ordinary look so beautifully extraordinary!  Congratulations!<br/></td>', 'Of COURSE this won.. and of COURSE its yours.  Irene, what a gift to be able to make the ordinary look so beautifully extraordinary!  Congratulations!', '2020-04-13 12:08:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(7658357, 1247452, 24454, '<td valign="top">Its perfection!   Your little Mo did an amazing job modeling!  Even if he had to be bribed!</td>', 'Its perfection!   Your little Mo did an amazing job modeling!  Even if he had to be bribed!', '2020-04-13 12:11:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7658367, 1247452, 86447, '<td valign="top">What a bunch of CROCK!!<br/> <br/>(and kitty!)<br/> <br/>Well done, Wendy!<br/>(again)<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your RIBBON!!<br/></td>', 'What a bunch of CROCK!! (and kitty!) Well done, Wendy!(again) Congratulations on your RIBBON!!', '2020-04-13 12:24:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(7658378, 1247452, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vawendy:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roz:</b></div><hr/><i> you and Irene got my highest scores .. two of my favourites in the challenge . there were a couple of others i really really liked that didnt do so well tho .. <br/>anyway .. many congratulations on such a brilliant image .. <br/>its truly a magic shot .. will be looking forward to finding out how you did this . <br/>are you a cat whisperer by any chance .. <br/>and is cat whispering something you can learn .. and can it be converted to dog whispering .. xx </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hehe -- no secret -- It is a very large crock. <br/> <br/>The difficult part was that Mo didn''t want to go in the crock. Jeff finally picked him up and put him in it. Once he realized that there was some canned chicken in the bottom, he didn''t mind as much. However, then he would completely disappear. When he was tired of the chicken, he would look out and get out right away. I think I only had 2-3 usable shots from about 25 minutes of shooting! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thanks Wendy .. you are very patient creative imaginative and cat friendly .. xx</td>', 'Originally posted by vawendy: Originally posted by roz: you and Irene got my highest scores .. two of my favourites in the challenge . there were a couple of others i really really liked that didnt do so well tho .. anyway .. many congratulations on such a brilliant image .. its truly a magic shot .. will be looking forward to finding out how you did this . are you a cat whisperer by any chance .. and is cat whispering something you can learn .. and can it be converted to dog whispering .. xx   Hehe -- no secret -- It is a very large crock.  The difficult part was that Mo didn''t want to go in the crock. Jeff finally picked him up and put him in it. Once he realized that there was some canned chicken in the bottom, he didn''t mind as much. However, then he would completely disappear. When he was tired of the chicken, he would look out and get out right away. I think I only had 2-3 usable shots from about 25 minutes of shooting!   thanks Wendy .. you are very patient creative imaginative and cat friendly .. xx', '2020-04-13 15:14:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(7658433, 1247452, 52549, '<td valign="top">Well done, Wendy, it''s a fantastic shot.</td>', 'Well done, Wendy, it''s a fantastic shot.', '2020-04-14 04:18:11.000000', NULL, 0),
